# Regression fixture for `export` (Rodada Exportação): the free
# parameter is named `E` -- a real coordinate/parameter name a user
# could plausibly choose (energy scale, eccentricity, ...) that happens
# to collide with BOTH Mathematica's own `E` (Euler's number) and
# SymPy's own `E`/`exp(1)` special constant. `export` must detect this
# and rename it (never silently emit code that would shadow the real
# constant), documenting the rename in its own output -- see
# `oderom_expr::export::{MATHEMATICA_RESERVED, SYMPY_RESERVED}`.
manifold M dim 2
bundle TM on M dim 2
chart c on M coords (t, r)
metric g on c bundle TM {
  [t,t] = -(1 - E/r),
  [r,r] = 1/(1 - E/r)
}
